      },
      "text": "SHERRY CASK (European oak, Quercus robur or sessilflora)\n  PX (Pedro Ximenez): very sweet sherry -> dried fruit, chocolate, Christmas cake\n  Oloroso: oxidized dry sherry -> nut, orange peel, complexity\n  First-fill vs second-fill: first-fill more flavor extraction\n  Expensive: sherry butts (500L) command premium; some European casks made new\n             and seasoned with sherry for purpose\n  Examples: Macallan (sherry cask dominant), Glendronach"
