      "text": "SINGLE POT STILL WHISKEY (uniquely Irish)\n  Mix of malted AND unmalted barley in same mash\n  Copper pot still distillation\n  Unmalted barley: grainy, spicy, oily character (\"pot still character\")\n  Triple distillation standard (though not legally required)\n  Most revived post-Troubles of Irish distilling industry\n  Examples: Redbreast, Green Spot, Yellow Spot, Powers (Jameson blend)"
    },
